# React Coding Standards

> **Project:** FlowPilot Frontend  
> **Framework:** React 19 + TypeScript + Vite  
> **Architecture:** Feature-Based Architecture  
> **UI:** Tailwind CSS v4 + shadcn/ui  
> **State Management:** TanStack Query + Zustand  
> **Routing:** React Router  
> **Workflow Canvas:** React Flow

---

# 2. Folder Organization

Organize code by **feature**, not by file type.

âœ… Good

```text
features/
    workflow/
        api/
        components/
        hooks/
        pages/
        store/
```

âŒ Avoid

```text
components/
pages/
hooks/
services/
```

for the entire application.

---

# 3. Naming Convention

## Components

Use **PascalCase**.

```tsx
WorkflowCard.tsx

ExecutionTable.tsx

NodeLibrary.tsx
```

---

## Hooks

Prefix with `use`.

```tsx
useWorkflow.ts

usePublishWorkflow.ts

useNodeSelection.ts
```

---

## Services

Use camelCase.

```tsx
workflow.service.ts

execution.service.ts
```

---

## API

```tsx
workflow.api.ts

connector.api.ts
```

---

## Store

```tsx
auth.store.ts

designer.store.ts
```

---

## Utils

```tsx
formatDate.ts

parseCron.ts

downloadFile.ts
```

---

## Types

```tsx
workflow.ts

execution.ts

connector.ts
```

---

# 4. Component Guidelines

A component should:

- Have one responsibility
- Be reusable
- Stay under ~200 lines whenever possible
- Move complex logic into hooks

Bad

```tsx
WorkflowPage
    700 lines
```

Good

```text
WorkflowPage

â”œâ”€â”€ WorkflowTable
â”œâ”€â”€ WorkflowToolbar
â”œâ”€â”€ CreateWorkflowDialog
â”œâ”€â”€ DeleteWorkflowDialog
```

---

# 5. Props

Always define interfaces.

```tsx
interface WorkflowCardProps {
    workflow: Workflow;
    onDelete: () => void;
}
```

Avoid

```tsx
function WorkflowCard(props: any)
```

---

# 6. TypeScript

Never use

```tsx
any
```

Use

```tsx
unknown
```

or proper interfaces.

Prefer

```tsx
interface Workflow
```

